    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0703" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2055: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Jenkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-04-30T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 30,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>For Johnson from Stevens.</p>
                <p>“Your April 18, 4 [<hi rendition="#italic">5</hi>] p.m.<anchor n="95"
                        xml:id="d538-f1"/> Technical Board should issue positive instructions to
                    railway management to make no payments whatever except such as authorized by
                    Board. Copy of these instructions should be handed Chinese member of Board for
                    transmission to his Government.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d538-f1" n="95" xml:id="d538-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram, Apr. 18, addressed to the Secretary of State, <ref target="#pg577"
                        >p. 577</ref>.</p>
            </note>
